      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling that you are fundamentally broken is a symptom of the pain, not the truth of who you are. Healing from something this deep isn't about erasing the mistake, but about learning to live with the weight of it while still being human. A therapist can provide tools to process guilt and shame, helping you move from self-punishment to understanding and repair. Remember that your worth is not determined by the worst thing you've ever done.",
      "source": "target",
